`applyServiceReply` is a pure state transition. Validate that `state.token` is either a string or `null`, `state.screen` is a string, `reply.status` is an integer from 100 through 599, and `reply.message` is a string; otherwise throw `TypeError`. Never mutate or return the input state object. For status 200 through 299, return a fresh copy with `alert: null`. For other statuses, set `alert` to `reply.message` when non-empty, otherwise `Request failed (<status>)`. Clear the token and change the screen to `catalog` only for status 401 or the exact message `SESSION_REVOKED`; if already on `catalog`, it remains there. All other fields retain their input values.

